\section*{Source and verification scope}
The counts in this section describe the historical analytic export. The
separately integrated de Jong theorem has its own fixed source and
verification record, linked from \texttt{docs/DEJONG.md}, and is not included
in those counts.
The 534 synchronized chapters and complete original statement/proof extracts
contain 1,918 nonempty original proof environments. Their 5,215 distinct
declaration reference spellings comprise 4,972 local bindings, 241 upstream-only
bindings and 2 explicitly unresolved historical attachment names. The full
document has 619 chapter inputs, 2,389 nonempty proof environments and 6,131 distinct
local binding spellings. These source counts are separate from compiled Lean
binding checks and the final publication gates recorded in the audit receipts.

The fixed accepted native continuation has 443 chapters, 1,340 labelled nodes,
1,325 complete proof environments and 52 labelled definitions; 15 definitions
have no separate proof environment. Every labelled non-definition in that
native inventory, and all 48 labelled statements in the 16 complete original
chapters and two complete original statement/proof extracts added by this
increment, have a following complete proof. The one labelled definition in
this increment also has a complete proof environment.
The full historical document retains 36 findings from the strict statement-scope
inspector, including five in the synchronized union. These concern historical
label coverage or missing statement proofs and are listed individually in the
audit; no claim that every historical attachment has a complete proof is made.

Local bindings use \texttt{lean} metadata; upstream-only facts use
\texttt{upstreamlean}, and unresolved historical names use
\texttt{upstreamunbound}. The current published source revision is
\texttt{6a888f9dc4155b9ec1407b27223eb37218957159} in
\href{https://github.com/MingchenXia/archon-nakamaye}{MingchenXia/archon-nakamaye},
corresponding to the accepted native checkpoint
\texttt{4774cd3a97737754b463603a2188df4cd48efd84}.
The per-checkpoint reports identify earlier fixed source revisions and the
complete source, binding and namespace provenance. The full document also
retains the earlier original extension chapters.
\input{dejong-alterations}
\section{Prerequisites from the original API}
These results use the embedded resolution theorems already proved in the library.
The following pointers identify the earlier results referred to in the proofs below.
\subsection{Pure-dimensional embedded resolution}\label{hir:embedded-resolution-pure-dimensional}
See \texttt{Hironaka.exists\_embeddedResolution\_pure\_of\_isCompact} and its compact-ambient and relatively compact variants in \texttt{API} and \texttt{API2}.
\subsection{Embedded resolution with an SNC boundary}\label{hir:embedded-resolution-boundary}
See \texttt{Hironaka.exists\_embeddedResolution\_boundary\_of\_isCompact} and the corresponding variants in \texttt{API2}.
\subsection{Embedded resolution in mixed dimensions}\label{hir:embedded-resolution-analytic}
See \texttt{Hironaka.exists\_embeddedResolution\_analytic\_of\_isCompact} and its boundary form in \texttt{API3}.
